<title>USA: Amer Radio to sell station for $27.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Amer Radio to sell station for $27.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Radio Systems Corp said on Monday that it has reached an agreement to sell radio station KXOA-FM in Sacramento, California to Entercom for $27.5 million.</p>
<p>The company said it expects the sale to be finalized during the first half of 1997, subject to the approval of the Federal Communications Commission.</p>
